      "source": [
        "# ✅ Climate Data Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "**Notebook 3 of 3: Validating Processed Climate Data**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 📋 Purpose\n",
        "This notebook validates the processed climate data against:\n",
        "- Expected UK climate ranges\n",
        "- CIBSE Guide A design data (UK building design standards)\n",
        "- Met Office UK climate averages\n",
        "- Internal consistency checks\n",
        "\n",
        "## 🎯 Validation Objectives\n",
        "1. Verify data is within expected ranges for UK climate\n",
        "2. Compare design temperatures with CIBSE guidelines\n",
        "3. Validate HDD values against Degree Days.net\n",
        "4. Check for data quality issues (gaps, outliers)\n",
        "5. Generate validation report with visualizations\n",
        "\n",
        "## 📊 Data Sources for Validation\n",
        "- [CIBSE Guide A: Environmental Design](https://www.cibse.org/knowledge/knowledge-items/detail?article=Guide_A_Environmental_design)\n",
        "- [Met Office UK Climate Averages](https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/research/climate/maps-and-data/uk-and-regional-series)\n",
        "- [Degree Days.net](https://www.degreedays.net/)\n",
        "\n",
        "## 🔗 Dependencies\n",
        "- pandas\n",
        "- numpy\n",
        "- matplotlib\n",
        "- seaborn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Install visualization dependencies\n",
        "!pip install matplotlib seaborn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Import libraries\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from datetime import datetime\n",
        "import warnings\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Set up matplotlib\n",
        "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')\n",
        "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (12, 6)\n",
        "plt.rcParams['font.size'] = 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📁 Setup and Load Data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Define directories\n",
        "PROCESSED_DATA_DIR = '../data/climate/processed'\n",
        "MONTHLY_DATA_DIR = '../data/climate/monthly'\n",
        "METADATA_PATH = '../data/climate/uk_cities_metadata.csv'\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load city metadata\n",
        "cities_df = pd.read_csv(METADATA_PATH)\n",
        "cities = cities_df.to_dict('records')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load all processed data\n",
        "processed_files = [f for f in os.listdir(PROCESSED_DATA_DIR) if f.endswith('_processed.csv')]\n",
        "processed_files.sort()\n",
        "\n",
        "data = {}\n",
        "for f in processed_files:\n",
        "    city_name = f.replace('_2014-2024_hourly_processed.csv', '').replace('_', ' ').title()\n",
        "    df = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(PROCESSED_DATA_DIR, f), parse_dates=['time'], index_col='time')\n",
        "    data[city_name] = df\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f'✅ Loaded {len(data)} cities from processed data')\n",
        "print(f'📁 Cities: {list(data.keys())}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🏗️ Climate Data Validator Class\n",
        "A reusable class for validating climate data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class ClimateDataValidator:\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Validates climate data against expected ranges and standards.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Expected ranges for UK climate\n",
        "    UK_CLIMATE_RANGES = {\n",
        "        'temp': {'min': -15, 'max': 40, 'avg_min': -5, 'avg_max': 30},\n",
        "        'rhum': {'min': 0, 'max': 100, 'avg_min': 50, 'avg_max': 90},\n",
        "        'wspd': {'min': 0, 'max': 50, 'avg_min': 0, 'avg_max': 25},\n",
        "        'pres': {'min': 950, 'max': 1050, 'avg_min': 980, 'avg_max': 1030},\n",
        "        'solar_rad': {'min': 0, 'max': 1200, 'avg_min': 0, 'avg_max': 800},\n",
        "        'precip': {'min': 0, 'max': 100, 'avg_min': 0, 'avg_max': 50}\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # CIBSE design temperatures for UK cities (approximate)\n",
        "    # Source: CIBSE Guide A: Environmental Design\n",
        "    CIBSE_DESIGN_TEMPS = {\n",
        "        'London': {'winter': -3.0, 'summer': 31.0},\n",
        "        'Manchester': {'winter': -5.0, 'summer': 28.0},\n",
        "        'Birmingham': {'winter': -5.0, 'summer': 29.0},\n",
        "        'Leeds': {'winter': -6.0, 'summer': 28.0},\n",
        "        'Glasgow': {'winter': -7.0, 'summer': 27.0},\n",
        "        'Edinburgh': {'winter': -7.0, 'summer': 26.0},\n",
        "        'Cardiff': {'winter': -4.0, 'summer': 29.0},\n",
        "        'Belfast': {'winter': -5.0, 'summer': 27.0},\n",
        "        'Bristol': {'winter': -4.0, 'summer': 29.0},\n",
        "        'Newcastle': {'winter': -7.0, 'summer': 27.0},\n",
        "        'Lerwick': {'winter': -8.0, 'summer': 23.0}  # Shetland Islands\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Expected HDD ranges for UK cities (annual)\n",
        "    # Source: Degree Days.net\n",
        "    EXPECTED_HDD = {\n",
        "        'London': (2000, 2500),\n",
        "        'Manchester': (2500, 3000),\n",
        "        'Birmingham': (2400, 2800),\n",
        "        'Leeds': (2600, 3100),\n",
        "        'Glasgow': (2800, 3300),\n",
        "        'Edinburgh': (2800, 3300),\n",
        "        'Cardiff': (2000, 2500),\n",
        "        'Belfast': (2500, 3000),\n",
        "        'Bristol': (2000, 2500),\n",
        "        'Newcastle': (2800, 3300),\n",
        "        'Lerwick': (3200, 3700)  # Shetland Islands - higher HDD\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def __init__(self):\n",
        "        pass\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def validate_ranges(self, df: pd.DataFrame, city_name: str) -> dict:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Validate that data is within expected ranges.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        results = {}\n",
        "        \n",
        "        for param, expected in self.UK_CLIMATE_RANGES.items():\n",
        "            if param in df.columns:\n",
        "                param_results = {\n",
        "                    'min': float(df[param].min()),\n",
        "                    'max': float(df[param].max()),\n",
        "                    'mean': float(df[param].mean()),\n",
",
        "                    'expected_min': expected['min'],\n",
        "                    'expected_max': expected['max'],\n",
        "                    'in_range': True\n",
        "                }\n",
        "                \n",
        "                # Check if values are within expected range\n",
        "                if df[param].min() < expected['min'] or df[param].max() > expected['max']:\n",
        "                    param_results['in_range'] = False\n",
        "                    param_results['warning'] = f'Values outside range [{expected["min"]}, {expected["max"]}]'\n",
        "                \n",
        "                # Check if average is within expected average range\n",
        "                if 'avg_min' in expected and 'avg_max' in expected:\n",
        "                    if df[param].mean() < expected['avg_min'] or df[param].mean() > expected['avg_max']:\n",
        "                        param_results['in_range'] = False\n",
        "                        param_results['warning'] = f'Average outside expected range [{expected["avg_min"]}, {expected["avg_max"]}]'\n",
        "                \n",
        "                results[param] = param_results\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return results\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def validate_design_temps(self, design_temps: dict, city_name: str) -> dict:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Compare calculated design temperatures with CIBSE guidelines.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        # Get CIBSE values for this city\n",
        "        cibse = self.CIBSE_DESIGN_TEMPS.get(city_name, {})\n",
        "        \n",
        "        results = {\n",
        "            'calculated_winter': design_temps.get('winter_design_temp'),\n",
        "            'cibse_winter': cibse.get('winter'),\n",
",
        "            'calculated_summer': design_temps.get('summer_design_temp'),\n",
        "            'cibse_summer': cibse.get('summer'),\n",
        "            'winter_match': None,\n",
        "            'summer_match': None,\n",
        "            'notes': ''\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Compare winter design temperatures\n",
        "        if results['calculated_winter'] is not None and results['cibse_winter'] is not None:\n",
        "            # Allow ±2°C tolerance for design temperatures\n",
        "            if abs(results['calculated_winter'] - results['cibse_winter']) <= 2:\n",
        "                results['winter_match'] = True\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                results['winter_match'] = False\n",
        "                results['notes'] += f'Winter design temp differs from CIBSE by {abs(results["calculated_winter"] - results["cibse_winter"]):.1f}°C. '\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Compare summer design temperatures\n",
        "        if results['calculated_summer'] is not None and results['cibse_summer'] is not None:\n",
        "            if abs(results['calculated_summer'] - results['cibse_summer']) <= 2:\n",
        "                results['summer_match'] = True\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                results['summer_match'] = False\n",
        "                results['notes'] += f'Summer design temp differs from CIBSE by {abs(results["calculated_summer"] - results["cibse_summer"]):.1f}°C.'\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return results\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def validate_hdd(self, df: pd.DataFrame, city_name: str) -> dict:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Validate HDD values against expected ranges.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        expected_range = self.EXPECTED_HDD.get(city_name, (2000, 3500))\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Calculate average annual HDD\n",
        "        if 'hdd_annual' in df.columns:\n",
        "            avg_hdd = df.groupby(df.index.year)['hdd_annual'].mean().mean()\n",
        "        elif 'hdd_daily' in df.columns:\n",
        "            avg_hdd = df['hdd_daily'].sum() / len(df.index.year.unique())\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            avg_hdd = None\n",
        "        \n",
        "        results = {\n",
        "            'calculated_hdd': avg_hdd,\n",
        "            'expected_min': expected_range[0],\n",
        "            'expected_max': expected_range[1],\n",
        "            'in_range': None,\n",
        "            'notes': ''\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        \n",
        "        if avg_hdd is not None:\n",
        "            if expected_range[0] <= avg_hdd <= expected_range[1]:\n",
        "                results['in_range'] = True\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                results['in_range'] = False\n",
        "                results['notes'] = f'HDD {avg_hdd:.0f} outside expected range [{expected_range[0]}, {expected_range[1]}]°C·days'\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return results\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def check_data_quality(self, df: pd.DataFrame) -> dict:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Check data quality metrics.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        results = {\n",
        "            'total_records': len(df),\n",
        "            'expected_records': 10 * 365.25 * 24,  # 10 years of hourly data\n",
",
        "            'completeness_pct': (len(df) / (10 * 365.25 * 24)) * 100,\n",
        "            'missing_values': df.isnull().sum().to_dict(),\n",
",
        "            'duplicate_records': df.duplicated().sum(),\n",
",
        "            'date_range': {\n",
        "                'start': df.index.min(),\n",
        "                'end': df.index.max()\n",
        "            }\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Check for gaps in data\n",
        "        time_diff = df.index.to_series().diff()\n",
        "        gaps = (time_diff > pd.Timedelta(hours=2)).sum()\n",
        "        results['gaps'] = gaps\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return results\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def validate_city(self, df: pd.DataFrame, city_name: str, design_temps: dict = None) -> dict:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Full validation for a single city.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        results = {\n",
        "            'city': city_name,\n",
        "            'range_validation': self.validate_ranges(df, city_name),\n",
",
        "            'data_quality': self.check_data_quality(df)\n",
",
        "        }\n",
        "        \n",
        "        if design_temps:\n",
        "            results['design_temp_validation'] = self.validate_design_temps(design_temps, city_name)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        results['hdd_validation'] = self.validate_hdd(df, city_name)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return results\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def generate_validation_report(self, validation_results: dict) -> dict:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Generate a summary validation report.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        report = {\n",
        "            'total_cities': len(validation_results),\n",
",
        "            'passed_cities': [],\n",
",
        "            'failed_cities': [],\n",
",
        "            'warnings': [],\n",
",
        "            'summary': {}\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        \n",
        "        for city_name, results in validation_results.items():\n",
        "            city_passed = True\n",
        "            city_warnings = []\n",
        "            \n",
        "            # Check range validation\n",
        "            for param, param_results in results['range_validation'].items():\n",
        "                if not param_results.get('in_range', True):\n",
        "                    city_passed = False\n",
        "                    city_warnings.append(f'{param}: {param_results.get("warning", "Out of range")}')\n",
        "            \n",
        "            # Check design temperature validation\n",
        "            if 'design_temp_validation' in results:\n",
        "                dt_validation = results['design_temp_validation']\n",
        "                if not dt_validation.get('winter_match') or not dt_validation.get('summer_match'):\n",
        "                    city_warnings.append(dt_validation.get('notes', 'Design temp mismatch'))\n",
        "            \n",
        "            # Check HDD validation\n",
        "            hdd_validation = results['hdd_validation']\n",
        "            if not hdd_validation.get('in_range'):\n",
        "                city_warnings.append(hdd_validation.get('notes', 'HDD out of range'))\n",
        "            \n",
        "            # Check data quality\n",
        "            dq = results['data_quality']\n",
        "            if dq['completeness_pct'] < 80:\n",
        "                city_passed = False\n",
        "                city_warnings.append(f'Data completeness: {dq["completeness_pct"]:.1f}% (< 80%)')\n",
        "            \n",
        "            if dq['gaps'] > 100:\n",
        "                city_warnings.append(f'Data gaps: {dq["gaps"]} gaps detected')\n",
        "            \n",
        "            if city_passed:\n",
        "                report['passed_cities'].append(city_name)\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                report['failed_cities'].append(city_name)\n",
        "            \n",
        "            if city_warnings:\n",
        "                report['warnings'].append({\n",
        "                    'city': city_name,\n",
        "                    'warnings': city_warnings\n",
        "                })\n",
        "        \n",
        "        report['summary'] = {\n",
        "            'pass_rate': len(report['passed_cities']) / len(validation_results) * 100,\n",
        "            'total_warnings': len(report['warnings'])\n",
",
        "        }\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return report"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🚀 Run Validation for All Cities"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Initialize validator\n",
        "validator = ClimateDataValidator()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load design temperatures from processed data\n",
        "# (These were calculated in Notebook 2)\n",
        "design_temps_data = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "# We'll extract design temps from the processed data\n",
        "for city_name, df in data.items():\n",
        "    if not df.empty:\n",
        "        design_temps_data[city_name] = {\n",
        "            'winter_design_temp': float(df['temp'].quantile(0.01)),\n",
        "            'summer_design_temp': float(df['temp'].quantile(0.99)),\n",
        "            'avg_temp': float(df['temp'].mean()),\n",
        "            'min_temp': float(df['temp'].min()),\n",
        "            'max_temp': float(df['temp'].max())\n",
        "        }\n",
        "\n",
        "print('🔍 Running validation for all cities...')\n",
        "print('=' * 60)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Run validation for each city\n",
        "from tqdm import tqdm\n",
        "\n",
        "validation_results = {}\n",
        "for city_name, df in tqdm(data.items(), desc='Validating cities'):\n",
        "    if not df.empty:\n",
        "        dt = design_temps_data.get(city_name, None)\n",
        "        validation_results[city_name] = validator.validate_city(df, city_name, dt)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        print(f'⚠️  No data for {city_name}')\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f'✅ Validated {len(validation_results)}/{len(data)} cities')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Generate validation report\n",
        "report = validator.generate_validation_report(validation_results)\n",
        "\n",
        "print('=' * 60)\n",
        "print('📊 VALIDATION REPORT SUMMARY')\n",
        "print('=' * 60)\n",
        "print(f'Total Cities Validated: {report["total_cities"]}')\n",
        "print(f'Passed: {len(report["passed_cities"])}')\n",
        "print(f'Failed: {len(report["failed_cities"])}')\n",
        "print(f'Pass Rate: {report["summary"]["pass_rate"]:.1f}%')\n",
        "print(f'Total Warnings: {report["summary"]["total_warnings"]}')\n",
        "\n",
        "if report['passed_cities']:\n",
        "    print('\\n✅ PASSED CITIES:')\n",
        "    for city in report['passed_cities']:\n",
        "        print(f'   - {city}')\n",
        "\n",
        "if report['failed_cities']:\n",
        "    print('\\n❌ FAILED CITIES:')\n",
        "    for city in report['failed_cities']:\n",
        "        print(f'   - {city}')\n",
        "\n",
        "if report['warnings']:\n",
        "    print('\\n⚠️  WARNINGS:')\n",
        "    for warning in report['warnings']:\n",
        "        print(f'\\n   {warning["city"]}:')\n",
        "        for w in warning['warnings']:\n",
        "            print(f'      - {w}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📊 Visualization 1: Temperature Comparison Across Cities"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Create comparison DataFrame for average temperatures\n",
        "avg_temps = []\n",
        "for city_name, df in data.items():\n",
        "    if not df.empty:\n",
        "        avg_temps.append({\n",
        "            'City': city_name,\n",
        "            'Avg Temp (°C)': df['temp'].mean(),\n",
        "            'Min Temp (°C)': df['temp'].min(),\n",
        "            'Max Temp (°C)': df['temp'].max()\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "avg_temp_df = pd.DataFrame(avg_temps).sort_values('Avg Temp (°C)', ascending=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 6))\n",
        "sns.barplot(data=avg_temp_df, x='City', y='Avg Temp (°C)', color='steelblue')\n",
        "plt.title('Average Temperature by City (2014-2024)', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Temperature (°C)')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('City')\n",
        "plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
        "plt.grid(axis='y', alpha=0.3)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display the data\n",
        "display(avg_temp_df)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📊 Visualization 2: Heating Degree Days (HDD) Comparison"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Create HDD comparison DataFrame\n",
        "hdd_data = []\n",
        "for city_name, df in data.items():\n",
        "    if not df.empty and 'hdd_annual' in df.columns:\n",
        "        avg_hdd = df.groupby(df.index.year)['hdd_annual'].mean().mean()\n",
        "        hdd_data.append({\n",
        "            'City': city_name,\n",
        "            'Avg Annual HDD (°C·days)': avg_hdd\n",
        "        })\n",
        "    elif not df.empty and 'hdd_daily' in df.columns:\n",
        "        avg_hdd = df['hdd_daily'].sum() / len(df.index.year.unique())\n",
        "        hdd_data.append({\n",
        "            'City': city_name,\n",
        "            'Avg Annual HDD (°C·days)': avg_hdd\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "hdd_df = pd.DataFrame(hdd_data).sort_values('Avg Annual HDD (°C·days)', ascending=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 6))\n",
        "colors = ['darkred' if city in ['Lerwick', 'Newcastle', 'Glasgow', 'Edinburgh'] else 'lightcoral' for city in hdd_df['City']]\n",
        "sns.barplot(data=hdd_df, x='City', y='Avg Annual HDD (°C·days)', palette=colors)\n",
        "plt.title('Average Annual Heating Degree Days by City (Base 15.5°C)', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('HDD (°C·days)')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('City')\n",
